# Environments
# `.env` alone matches ONLY that exact name, so a `.env.bak` / `.env.local` /
# editor swap file holding the same API key was stageable. Near-missed exactly
# that. `.env.*` closes it; the negation keeps the tracked template visible.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc
.venv
env/
venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

