# --- bias_steer: runs & coordinator (docs/02-architecture-roadmap.md §8, §10) ---
# Runs are committed by DEFAULT (never lose an experiment). Only these stay out of git.
# NOTE: .gitignore has no inline comments — patterns must stand alone on their own line.
#
# Bulky residual tensors (>100MB GitHub cap); regenerable from committed inputs:
runs/**/residuals.safetensors
# Un-ignore run event logs. The generic `*.log` rule above (line 62, from the
# stock Python/Django template) was silently swallowing every run's
# logs/run.log — the phase/timing/bucket-count event stream that §7.2 lists as
# part of a run's committed record. Observed: run.log was the ONLY file missing
# from committed runs, so bucket sizes were unrecoverable after a branch switch.
!runs/**/*.log
# Throwaway runs (opt-out pile):
runs/_discard/
# Ephemeral batch STATE (route/queue/control/status); coordinator CODE lives in
# src/bias_steer/ and IS committed:
_coordinator/

# --- third-party refusal-direction artifacts (fetched, not committed) ---
# Downloaded by scripts/fetch_refusal_artifacts.py; provenance in the pinned
# manifest.json. Only the manifest, README, and fetch script are committed.
third_party/refusal_direction/runs/
third_party/refusal_direction/dataset/

# Community Discord harvest — raw dumps have usernames/PII; keep local only
experiments/community_methods/raw/
experiments/community_methods/HARVEST_SUMMARY.json
# HARVEST_STATS.json / MINING_REPORT.md / method_cards.yaml are OK to commit

# Fusion workspace — holds the unpublished manuscript (a nested git repo whose
# origin is the Overleaf bridge, auth cached), the append-only claim ledger, and
# gate archives. None of it belongs in this repo. Was untracked-but-unignored,
# so a single `git add -A` would have published it.
.fusion-private/
.pi/

# Annotation pools contain model text + sealed arm keys — local only
experiments/annotation_pools/
